> sw1(x: u32) = x xor (x >> 16) xor (x >> 8) xor (x >> 4) xor (x >> 2) xor (x >> 1)
> sw2(x: u32) = ((x xor (x >> 16)) xor (x >> 8)) xor ((x >> 4) xor (x >> 2)) xor (x >> 1)
> equiv sw1 sw2
sw1 and sw2 are equal on the domain of sw1 (proved by SAT: 777 AIG nodes, 1705 conflicts)
> r1(x: u32, n: u32 in 1..31) = (x << n) | (x >> (32 - n))
> r2(x: u32, n: u32 in 1..31) = (x >> (32 - n)) | (x << n)
> equiv r1 r2
r1 and r2 are equal on the domain of r1 (proved by SAT: 1192 AIG nodes, 0 conflicts)
> fp(x: u32, y: u32) = (x + y) * (x - y)
> gq(x: u32, y: u32) = x*x - y*y
> equiv fp gq
fp and gq are equal on the domain of fp (proved by algebra: both sides expand to one polynomial in x, y mod 2^32)
